    <dashboard name='Story 2' type='storyboard'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='664' maxwidth='1716' minheight='664' minwidth='1716' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='97590' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99068' x='466' y='1205'>
            <zone h='6325' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99068' x='466' y='1205' />
            <zone h='15211' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99068' x='466' y='7530' />
            <zone h='76054' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99068' x='466' y='22741'>
              <flipboard active-id='1' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point captured-sheet='Sheet 2' id='1' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='50000' id='6' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='45338' x='17541' y='24096'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>This visualization shows the number of tourists visiting different countries every year. It helps us identify which countries are the most popular tourist destinations. Countries with very high visitor numbers usually have famous landmarks, strong tourism facilities, good transport, and global recognition.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Countries with average visitors show stable tourism performance, but they still have scope to grow by improving facilities and marketing. Countries with low visitors indicate hidden tourism potential. With better promotion, infrastructure, and tourist-friendly policies, these countries can attract more visitors in the future.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>This visual is useful for tourism planners, government bodies, and businesses to decide where to invest and which destinations need more promotion. </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{D9B1A4D5-5BB9-456C-8B37-4F78F1681D8D}' />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard name='Story 4' type='storyboard'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='664' maxwidth='1716' minheight='664' minwidth='1716' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='97590' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='99068' x='466' y='1205'>
            <zone h='6325' id='3' type-v2='title' w='99068' x='466' y='1205' />
            <zone h='15211' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='99068' x='466' y='7530' />
            <zone h='76054' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99068' x='466' y='22741'>
              <flipboard active-id='1' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point captured-sheet='Sheet 6' id='1' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='50000' id='6' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='40793' x='39802' y='31627'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>This visualization shows how entry fees differ based on the type of tourist attraction. Some attraction types charge higher fees because they offer premium services, special experiences, or require high maintenance. Examples include theme parks, museums, or special heritage sites.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Other attractions like natural places, public parks, or religious places usually have low or no entry fee so that more people can visit them easily. This shows that pricing strategy depends on the type of attraction and the kind of experience it provides.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>This chart helps us understand how tourism businesses balance between profit and accessibility. It also helps tourists choose destinations based on their budget and interest.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{1A3CFFC3-C148-4A82-893A-148D827DC86C}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
